Requirements: 7   with obligations: 7

[task-01] When the benchmark's instability measurement finishes, it prints the per-stage
    usage table that `acceptance check` and `acceptance decompose` already print,
    covering every model call the measurement made, with live and replayed calls counted
    apart.
    -> instability-measurement-prints-usage-table  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       When the benchmark's instability measurement finishes, it prints the same per-
       stage usage table that `acceptance check` and `acceptance decompose` already
       print.
    -> usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The per-stage usage table printed when the benchmark's instability measurement
       finishes accounts for every model call the measurement made, so that the table's
       totals equal the number of model calls issued during the measurement, with none
       omitted.
    -> usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The per-stage usage table printed at the end of the benchmark's instability
       measurement reports live model calls and replayed model calls as separate counts,
       rather than as a single combined figure.

[task-02] The table shows what the run spent on calls billed to Anthropic's own API
    separately from what it spent on any other provider, so the Anthropic credits a run
    consumed can be read off as a figure of its own. A call sent through the Message
    Batches API counts at the price it was billed at.
    -> table-separates-anthropic-spend  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The table presents the run's spend on calls billed to Anthropic's own API as a
       figure separate from the run's spend on calls billed to any other provider.
    -> anthropic-credits-own-figure  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The table presents the Anthropic credits consumed by a run as a distinct figure
       of its own, so a reader can read off the Anthropic total directly without
       deriving it from a combined total.
    -> batch-call-counted-at-billed-price  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A call sent through the Message Batches API is counted in the spend table at the
       price it was actually billed at, rather than at the standard (non-batch) price
       for that model.

[task-03] Which provider a call goes to is the one its configured model name states, and
    every part of the client that depends on the provider reads that one decision —
    whether a request carries cache breakpoints, whether it can be batched, and whose
    credits it spent — rather than each guessing from the model name in its own way.
    -> provider-routing-by-model-name  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Each call is routed to the provider that its configured model name states; the
       provider is derived from the configured model name and not from any other source.
    -> provider-decision-single-source  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Every part of the client that depends on the provider (whether a request carries
       cache breakpoints, whether it can be batched, and whose credits it spent) derives
       its behavior from the one resolved provider decision, not from its own
       interpretation of the configured model name.

[task-04] Spend stays out of the review state and the rendered report, as it is today.
    -> spend-excluded-from-review-state-and-report  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Keep spend data absent from both the review state and the rendered report, as it
       is today; the review state and the rendered report contain no spend information.

